# MAVILIVE Bodycam OBS Overlay

A transparent FiveM-style bodycam overlay and URL generator for OBS Browser Source.

## Features

- MAVILIVE branding
- Player Name field
- Department field
- Automatic `CIVILIAN` fallback when Department is empty
- Live preview
- Blinking red `REC` indicator
- Live date and time
- Generate OBS URL button
- Copy OBS URL button
- URL parameters
- No localStorage
- Single-file HTML
- Works as an OBS Browser Source

## Files

- `overlay.html` — main bodycam overlay and URL generator

## How to use

### 1. Upload

Upload `overlay.html` to your web hosting service.

For example:

`https://your-domain.com/overlay.html`

### 2. Open the page

Open the hosted `overlay.html` in your browser.

Enter:

- Player Name
- Department

If Department is empty, the overlay automatically uses:

`CIVILIAN`

### 3. Generate the OBS URL

Click:

`GENERATE OBS URL`

Then click:

`COPY OBS URL`

### 4. Add to OBS

In OBS:

1. Add a **Browser Source**.
2. Paste the generated URL.
3. Set the Browser Source resolution to match your stream, for example:
   - Width: `1920`
   - Height: `1080`
4. Leave the page background transparent.
5. Position the overlay where you want it on your FiveM stream.

## URL parameters

The overlay supports:

`?player=PlayerName&department=DepartmentName`

Example:

`https://your-domain.com/overlay.html?player=Mavi&department=Police`

Civilian example:

`https://your-domain.com/overlay.html?player=Mavi&department=CIVILIAN`

## Important

The URL must point to the publicly hosted `overlay.html` file for OBS to load it.

Do not use a local computer path such as:

`C:\Users\...\overlay.html`

Use the public HTTPS URL from your hosting provider.

## Customization

You can edit `overlay.html` to change:

- MAVILIVE branding
- Fonts
- Text sizes
- Positions
- REC animation
- Bodycam badge
- Colors
- Date/time format
- Preview appearance

## Privacy

This version does not use `localStorage`. Player and department information are stored only in the generated URL parameters.
